Slide 1 — Title
Bluestock Mutual Fund Analytics
End-to-End ETL, Performance & Risk Analytics

Capstone Project – Mutual Fund Analytics

Tools & Technologies:
Python | Pandas | SQL | SQLite | Power BI/Tableau | GitHub

Prepared by: Vamshi Yadav

Slide 2 — Problem & Objectives
Problem Statement

Mutual fund data is available across multiple datasets containing fund details, NAV history, investor transactions, performance, AUM, and benchmark information.

The project aims to transform this raw data into a clean, structured, and analytics-ready database for meaningful business insights.

Objectives
Build an automated ETL pipeline
Ingest and clean multiple CSV datasets
Validate data quality and consistency
Design an analytical SQLite database
Analyze mutual fund performance and risk
Analyze investor transaction behavior
Generate actionable insights
Prepare data for dashboard visualization
Slide 3 — Data Sources
Data Sources

The project uses 10 raw CSV datasets:

#	Dataset
01	Fund Master
02	NAV History
03	AUM by Fund House
04	Monthly SIP Inflows
05	Category Inflows
06	Industry Folio Count
07	Scheme Performance
08	Investor Transactions
09	Portfolio Holdings
10	Benchmark Indices
Processed Data
NAV records: 46,000
Investor transactions: 32,778
Performance records: 40
Mutual fund schemes: 40
