Slide 7 — Performance Metrics
Mutual Fund Performance Analysis

The project evaluates fund performance using multiple time horizons and benchmark comparisons.

Performance Metrics

1-Year Return
Measures recent fund performance.

3-Year Return
Provides a medium-term performance perspective.

5-Year Return
Helps evaluate longer-term consistency.

Alpha
Measures performance relative to the benchmark.

Benchmark Return
Provides a reference point for evaluating fund performance.

Analysis

Funds were compared using historical returns and benchmark-adjusted performance to identify stronger-performing schemes.

📌 Insert your performance comparison chart here.

Slide 8 — Risk Analysis
Risk & Risk-Adjusted Performance

The project evaluates both return and risk to provide a more complete view of fund quality.

Risk Metrics
Sharpe Ratio — Return relative to total risk
Sortino Ratio — Return relative to downside risk
Beta — Sensitivity to market movements
Standard Deviation — Measure of volatility
Maximum Drawdown — Largest historical decline
VaR — Potential loss at a selected confidence level
CVaR — Expected loss beyond VaR
Advanced Analytics

Rolling Sharpe Ratio analysis was performed to study how risk-adjusted performance changes over time.

📌 Insert your rolling_sharpe_chart.png here.

