Slide 11 — Key Findings & Recommendations
Key Findings
40 mutual fund schemes analyzed
46,000 NAV records processed
32,778 investor transactions analyzed
40 scheme performance records analyzed
Data quality checks completed successfully
No missing values were identified in the scheme performance dataset
No duplicate records were identified in the scheme performance dataset
No invalid expense-ratio records were detected
No extreme 1-year return anomalies were detected
Risk-adjusted performance was analyzed using Sharpe and Sortino ratios
Advanced VaR, CVaR and rolling Sharpe analysis was performed
Recommendations
Evaluate funds using both return and risk metrics
Compare fund returns against appropriate benchmarks
Monitor downside risk and maximum drawdown
Consider expense ratios when comparing similar funds
Evaluate long-term performance rather than relying only on 1-year returns
Use investor transaction trends to understand customer behavior
